INT. WILLOWBROOK FERTILITY CLINIC - WAITING ROOM - DAY

A pastel room. Gently glowing crystals on every table. A fountain BURBLES in the corner. A sign reads: "PLEASE SILENCE YOUR WANDS."

BRIDGET FENWICK, 30s, sits stiffly. Next to her, her husband, GARRETT, 30s, flips through a magazine upside down.

BRIDGET
(whispering, mortified)
Garrett, the magazine.

GARRETT
(turns it over, deadpan)
Oh, thank goodness. I was getting nothing out of the article.

The inner door swings open. Applause-ready.

DR. PLUM
(entering in a sparkly lab coat, arms wide)
The Fenwicks! Come in, come in, mind the dragon.

ANGLE ON a small green dragon asleep on the carpet, wearing a "Staff" lanyard.

GARRETT
(stepping over it)
Is that safe?

DR. PLUM
(cheerfully)
Mostly vegetarian.

INT. WILLOWBROOK FERTILITY CLINIC - EXAM ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Dr. Plum shuts the door. Bridget perches on the table. Garrett stays standing.

DR. PLUM
(clapping once)
Now, the good news is, your tests came back magical.

BRIDGET
(hopeful)
Magical how?

DR. PLUM
(checking a scroll)
Wonderfully magical. The bad news is, there's a small curse.

GARRETT
(flat)
There's always a small curse.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Dr. Plum, your two o'clock is here. And the stork is asking for a raise again.

DR. PLUM
(to the ceiling)
Tell him we'll discuss it in the spring, Winnie.

WINNIE (V.O.)
(from the intercom)
He says that's what you said last spring.

DR. PLUM
(muttering)
Storks.

CLOSE ON the scroll. Written in glittery cursive: "Hex of Perpetual Maybe."

BRIDGET
(reading it, aghast)
Perpetual Maybe?

DR. PLUM
(brightly)
Very common. Your great-aunt must've really wanted you to take your time.

GARRETT
(sighs, to Bridget)
This is your aunt Millicent.

BRIDGET
(tight smile)
She hated my first boyfriend, too.

DR. PLUM
(snaps fingers; a puff of glitter)
Good news! It's reversible. We'll start with a gentle exorcism.

GARRETT
(alarmed)
Gentle?

DR. PLUM
(already writing)
Light. Like a dentist.

BACK TO SCENE

The dragon pokes its head through the door.

DR. PLUM (CONT'D)
(not looking up)
Not now, Kevin.

The dragon sighs. A small puff of smoke. It leaves.
